course: dictionary
lesson: 1485
title: Cauliflower: a vegetable made of flower buds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a plant and also name the food we make from it. Look at the words around it to see which meaning is used. «Broccoli and cauliflower are flowers, and peas and beans are seeds» tells you that cauliflower is a plant part we eat.
explain: «From one wild cabbage plant, farmers bred cabbage, broccoli, cauliflower, kale and Brussels sprouts» shows that cauliflower is a plant that farmers grew and changed over time. It is a vegetable, not something made in a factory.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «We had cauliflower cheese for tea» works, because cauliflower here is food, like rice or bread. «A cauliflower grew in the garden» works too, because it means one whole plant.
fact: A cauliflower is a vegetable with a large, firm white head made of tiny flower buds, surrounded by green leaves.
fact: Cauliflower is in the cabbage family, with broccoli, kale and Brussels sprouts.
fact: Cauliflower is full of vitamin C and fibre, which help keep you healthy.
fact: Cauliflower cheese is a classic UK dish.
fact: Phrases such as cauliflower rice and cauliflower ear use the word in a new way, so check the context.
exercise: «Broccoli and cauliflower are flowers, and peas and beans are seeds.» Which plant part is cauliflower? | Stem | *Flower | Root | Seed
exercise: Farmers bred cauliflower from one wild cabbage plant. Which family does cauliflower belong to? | Carrot family | Grass family | Pea family | *Cabbage family
exercise: Which sentence uses cauliflower as food? | The farmer picked a cauliflower from the field | A cauliflower has a firm white head | The cauliflower grew a green leaf each day | *We had cauliflower cheese for tea
test: Cauliflower is full of which vitamin, along with fibre? | *Vitamin C | Vitamin D | Vitamin B12 | Vitamin K
test: Which vegetable is in the same family as cauliflower? | Lettuce | Potato | Carrot | *Brussels sprouts
exam: Which phrase describes a cauliflower as a vegetable? | Cauliflower cheese | Cauliflower ear | Cauliflower rice | *Large, firm white head of tiny flower buds
